    },
    {
      "id": "engines-8",
      "severity": "Bug",
      "summary": "both preprocessors crash on a formula holding the empty clause, Python with ValueError and native with a Rust panic that `except Exception` cannot catch, so `solve --preprocess -j 2` dies on any formula --preprocess refutes, instead of exiting 20"
    },
    {
      "id": "engines-9",
      "severity": "Bug",
      "summary": "a Config one engine accepts the other refuses: rnd_seed outside u32 and glue_keep < 0 raise OverflowError on native, an unknown restart or ccmin runs silently on Python; solve_adaptive also runs an unknown engine name as Python"
    }
  ],
  "not_checked": [
    "The default reduction, rephasing and restart-blocking thresholds are crossed only by the one 205-variable instance, where the oracle gives no verdict: parity and dratify only. On tiny formulas they are reached by lowering the thresholds.",
    "Restart blocking (10,000 conflicts) is unreachable below that instance, so it is covered by one instance.",
    "Assumptions have no native counterpart in the binding, so they are checked on Python only, and `set_decision`, `new_var(polarity=...)` likewise.",
    "`solve_portfolio(timeout=...)` and `solve_adaptive(seconds=...)` beyond a deadline of 0: tiny formulas finish before any deadline could fire.",
    "The race itself: threads and processes answer whichever way they finish, so winner-dependent counts vary slightly between runs; every check holds per winner.",
    "`_worker` on the native engine is reached by calling it directly, because the driver always takes threads when native is built. The process path on native (no threaded portfolio in the module) is not exercised.",
    "An `--adaptive` run stopped by a deadline in the CLI: the CLI passes none.",
    "`luby_base=0` and `walk_interval=0`, which are not meaningful configurations.",
    "The crates.io dratify 0.1.10: this build embeds the checkout's dratify/rust.",
    "Counters the native binding does not expose (walks, walk_flips, simplifications, removed_clauses, removed_lits) are read on Python to prove reach, and not compared.",
    "`CDCLKIT_ENGINE=native` without the build: it is built here, so that error is not reached.",
    "drat-trim: these proofs are replayed by the oracle's flavours and dratify, not by it."
  ],
